0..80 Comment "//! Copy-on-write pays for a holder count it reads at every write, even when the"
81..160 Comment "//! string is held once. A write that reads no count is sound exactly where the"
161..239 Comment "//! string has one holder: there it writes what copy-on-write writes, and on a"
240..318 Comment "//! shared string it would write the buffer another string reads. So where the"
319..396 Comment "//! program states that a string is not copied for a scope, the count and its"
397..414 Comment "//! branch can go"
415..491 Comment "//! [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics], § 4:"
492..571 Comment "//! uniqueness-elided copies. The statement is a grade on the string: `var[1] s"
572..649 Comment "//! = e;` holds a string made where the hold stands, which nothing else holds"
650..729 Comment "//! while it is held, and the checker refuses a grade-one hold of a string that"
730..810 Comment "//! may have been copied. The items below show the write the grade licenses, and"
811..823 Comment "//! on what."
824..827 Comment "//!"
828..906 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]"
